---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Research — the questions behind the soulsystem"
  description="The research wing of impire.io: PRA, a machine that learns a world by living in it, and imps, agents that are aware cheaply and think rarely. Pre-registered gates, honest measurement, failures in the open."
  project="pra"
  active="research"
>
  <header class="hero hero--sub">
    <div class="copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">research · two open questions</p>
      <h1>The questions we haven't earned answers to yet.</h1>
      <p class="sub">
        The soulsystem is infrastructure you can run today. The research wing is the other
        half of the work: questions too big to promise, pursued in the open. Every ambition
        sits behind a named, pre-registered gate; claims carry evidence, and
        <b>only a measurement closes a debate</b>.
      </p>
      <p class="sub">
        Failures are published next to the wins — a result that only <em>looks</em> smart
        is treated as a bug in the test rig, not a success.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="prose" style="padding-bottom: 46px">
    <div class="wing">
      <article class="card" style="--a: var(--pra); --a-bright: var(--pra-bright)">
        <p class="eyebrow">pra · pose resolution architecture</p>
        <h3>An intelligence with no task.</h3>
        <p>
          An AI that learns a world by <b>doing</b>, not by being told — no labels, no
          dataset, no task you hand it. On simple worlds it provably works; on complex
          worlds it grabs the simplest explanation instead of the true one. That gap is the
          headline question the whole project exists to answer.
        </p>
        <p class="links-row">
          <a class="enter enter--solid" href="/pra/">Meet PRA →</a>
          <a class="enter" href="https://impire.io/poseres-book/">The book (draft)</a>
          <a class="enter" href="/pra/how-it-works.html">See it live</a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="card" style="--a: var(--imps); --a-bright: var(--imps-bright)">
        <p class="eyebrow">imps · autonomous agents</p>
        <h3>An agent you don't drive.</h3>
        <p>
          Small agents that are <b>aware of everything cheaply and think rarely</b> — the
          awareness/thinking boundary enforced by the compiler, not by discipline. Early:
          two features shipped, the always-on cooperating colony is the direction, not the
          current state.
        </p>
        <p class="links-row">
          <a class="enter enter--solid" href="/imps/">Meet imps →</a>
          <a class="enter" href="https://github.com/impire-io/imps">The code</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h3>How research is run here</h3>
    <p>
      The same discipline binds both projects. Research topics open with a pre-registration
      — what question, what would count as an answer, what would change our minds — and
      close by graduating to a design, an artifact, or an honest abandonment. Direction
      decisions record their reversal conditions when they are made, so a future turn is a
      clean, anticipated move instead of drift.
    </p>
    <p>
      The full logs are public: every episode, reversal, and measurement, numbered and kept
      next to the code at <a href="https://github.com/impire-io">github.com/impire-io</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wing {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: none;
    margin: 34px 0 14px;
  }
  .links-row { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .wing { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
